# Employee Work Upload Module - Install Notes

A completely separate module. Nothing in your existing Task Management
Controllers/Models/Views/tables was touched.

## 1. Database

Run once:

```
Database/employee_work_upload_schema.sql
```

Creates two **new** tables only: `employee_work_uploads`, `employee_work_upload_files`.
Does not alter `tasks`, `task_assignments`, or any existing table.

## 2. Files to drop in

```
Admin/Model/EmployeeWorkUploadModel.php
Admin/Controller/employeeworkuploadcontroller.php
Admin/View/Work Upload/work-uploads.php
Employee/View/Work Upload/work-upload.php
Employee/View/Work Upload/submission-history.php
```

These mirror your existing conventions exactly:
- Same `ConnectDb::getInstance()->getConnection()` / mysqli + prepared statements as `TaskModel.php`.
- Same admin/employee action-gating pattern as `mytaskcontroller.php` (single controller,
  `$adminActions` / `$employeeActions` arrays, `user_id` -> `trainers.id` conversion via
  `getTrainerIdByUserId()` for the employee session).
- Same Bootstrap 5 + Bootstrap Icons UI, same scrollable-modal CSS pattern used in
  `task-management.php` / `my-tasks.php`.

## 3. Path adjustments (only thing you need to check)

Each view has a `CONTROLLER` constant at the top of its `<script>` block — same pattern
your existing pages use ("adjust relative path to match your folder depth"). Given the
folder layout the spec asked for (`Admin/View/Work Upload/` and `Employee/View/Work Upload/`
as siblings of `Admin/Controller/`), the paths are pre-set to:

- `Admin/View/Work Upload/work-uploads.php` → `../../Controller/employeeworkuploadcontroller.php`
- `Employee/View/Work Upload/*.php` → `../../../Admin/Controller/employeeworkuploadcontroller.php`

Adjust if your actual `www/` layout differs (identical to how `task-management.php` and
`my-tasks.php` already say to do this).

Uploaded files land in `uploads/work_uploads/` (new folder, separate from
`uploads/task_files/`), same pattern as `saveAssignmentFile()` in your existing code.

## 4. Menu wiring (add, don't replace)

**Employee menu:** Dashboard | My Tasks | **Work Upload** | **Submission History**
Link the two new items to `work-upload.php` and `submission-history.php`.

**Admin menu:** Task Management | **Work Uploads**
Link to `Admin/View/Work Upload/work-uploads.php`.

## 5. Notifications

- Admin page shows a live "N New Work Uploads Pending" badge
  (`action=admin_pending_count`, counts `review_status = 'Pending'`).
- Employee side exposes `action=my_review_summary` (counts of Approved / Needs Revision /
  Rejected) if you want to surface a badge on the employee dashboard — wire it in wherever
  your dashboard widgets live.

## 6. Controller actions reference

| Action | Who | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `upload_submit` | Employee | Submit new work (multipart, `files[]`) |
| `upload_resubmit` | Employee | Edit + resubmit after "Needs Revision" |
| `my_uploads_list` | Employee | Submission History table |
| `my_upload_get` | Employee | View Details modal |
| `my_review_summary` | Employee | Badge counts |
| `admin_list` | Admin | Work Uploads table (filters: `review_status`, `employee_id`, `search`) |
| `admin_get` | Admin | Review modal detail |
| `admin_review` | Admin | Approve / Need Revision / Reject |
| `admin_pending_count` | Admin | Pending badge |

Allowed attachment types (enforced server-side, silently skips anything else):
`zip, pdf, doc, docx, png, jpg, jpeg, mp4` — no limit on file count.